// methodology.nv - the illustration of the agent step that the methodology keeps (state-machine-agent-step.alula.md, format 2.17), copied as it is into `cases/` with the extension
// `.txt` (its links are the links of the methodology's folder), compiled in for the tests that pin what the translator says about it; the same for its English twin and for the record of the
// machine "Meeting". The files `cases/*-names-217*.tsv` are the output of the reference script of the methodology (`check-alula-keywords.py`): the JSON names of the declarations.
module alula.machine_agent

/// The text of the illustration of the methodology (format 2.17, AL-51 ... AL-64, task 151): copied as it is.
export fn methodology_text() -> str => embed_str("cases/agent-step-methodology-217.alula.txt")

/// The text of the English twin of the illustration (state-machine-agent-step.en.alula.md, the same machine, row for row), copied as it is.
export fn methodology_en_text() -> str => embed_str("cases/agent-step-methodology-217.en.alula.txt")

/// The record of the machine "Meeting" of the methodology at the same state (30 states, 67 rows, 12 rows of ends, 29 data, 22 primitives, 14 rows of the names), copied as it is.
export fn meeting_217_text() -> str => embed_str("cases/meeting-methodology-217.alula.txt")
